+#### Testing Stateful PTFs
+
+The harness supports PTFs that declare state via `@StateHint`. State is injected into `eval()` based on the
+partition key of the input table, and is converted to its internal representation (`ArrayData`, `MapData`, or
+`RowData`) after each `eval()` call, so state serialization is exercised as part of the test.
+
+The following state categories are supported:
+
+- Scalar state (e.g. `INT`, `STRING`)
+- `ListView` state
+- `MapView` state
+- `Row` and POJO structured types
+
+{{< tabs "stateful" >}}
+{{< tab "Java" >}}
+```java
+@DataTypeHint("ROW<key STRING, count INT>")
+public class CountPTF extends ProcessTableFunction<Row> {
+  public void eval(
+    @ArgumentHint(ArgumentTrait.SET_SEMANTIC_TABLE) Row input,
+    @StateHint int count) {
+    count++;
+    collect(Row.of(input.getFieldAs("key"), count));
+  }
+}
+
+@Test
+void testStatefulPTF() throws Exception {
+  try (ProcessTableFunctionTestHarness<Row> harness =
+    ProcessTableFunctionTestHarness.ofClass(CountPTF.class)
+    .withTableArgument("input", DataTypes.of("ROW<key STRING>"))
+    .withPartitionBy("input", "key")
+    .build()) {
+
+    harness.processElement(Row.of("A"));
+    harness.processElement(Row.of("A"));
+
+    List<Row> output = harness.getOutput();
+    assertThat(output).containsExactly(Row.of("A", 1), Row.of("A", 2));
+  }
+}
+```
+{{< /tab >}}
+{{< /tabs >}}
+
+State TTL is not supported by the test harness.
+
